    "notes": "1. 'Total revenues and other income' is mapped to total_revenue, comprising Sales and other operating revenue, Income from equity affiliates, and Other income. 2. 'Total costs and other deductions' includes both operating and non-operating costs. For total_operating_cost, only the operational cost elements are selected: Crude oil and product purchases, Production and manufacturing expenses, Selling, general and administrative expenses, Depreciation and depletion, Exploration expenses, and Non-service pension/postretirement expense. 3. 'Other taxes and duties' (26,288 in 2024) is excluded from total_operating_cost as it is considered a non-income tax (e.g., property, excise, severance taxes) and is part of the broader 'Costs and other deductions' but not a core operating expense for income generation. 4. 'Interest expense' and 'Income tax expense' are mapped directly to their respective fields. 5. 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil' is mapped to net_income. 6. Supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., for Other income, Depreciation, Taxes) but do not alter the primary income statement line item totals used for extraction. 7. Numbers in parentheses in the source are treated as negative values, but per rule 13, for taxes, interest_expenses, and total_operating_cost, the sign convention is reversed for the extraction: values that reduce income are reported as positive numbers. All extracted values are positive as they represent expense outflows.",
